Error [jet.UseAfterMove]: `res` was consumed by the struct literal, so it can't be used here
  --> tests/ui/ownership/close_value_copied_into_two_struct_literals_is_rejected.jet:12:59
    |
 12 |     pair: Pair{left: Holder{res: res}, right: Holder{res: res}}
    |                                                           ^^^
  --> tests/ui/ownership/close_value_copied_into_two_struct_literals_is_rejected.jet:12:34
    |
 12 |     pair: Pair{left: Holder{res: res}, right: Holder{res: res}}
    |                                  ^^^ `res` moved to the struct literal here
 Why: After a value moves somewhere else, its old name no longer gives access to it
 Fix: Stop using `res` after the move, or give the struct literal a copy with `res.copy()` where it moved.
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0121
